                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd5af2ce-dcf2-3226-9df2-63b8941200e0",
                        "entry_id": "90fce422-3454-3d14-ad82-b2bea773b980",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a la forme d’une plume."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8841d271-937d-4831-9631-4727966c2629",
                                "sense_id": "fd5af2ce-dcf2-3226-9df2-63b8941200e0",
                                "text": "PENNIFORME, adject., penniformis (penna, plume, forma, forme) ; qui a la forme d’une plume. Martius [Carl Friedrich Philipp von Martius] donne cette épithète aux rameaux à feuilles alternes, qu’on regarde communément comme des pétioles, parce qu’ils ont la forme et l’apparence de feuilles ailées (ex. Phyllanthus cochinchinensis). Candolle [Augustin Pyrame de Candolle] l’applique également aux feuilles qui sont disposées comme des feuilles pennées (ex. Hypopterygium penniforme)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad8acf16-1867-3d7c-84bd-bc2757b22273",
                        "entry_id": "90fce422-3454-3d14-ad82-b2bea773b980",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dont les tendons se dirigent vers une même structure et adopte une forme de plume."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd0c0897-70e4-48e7-a316-4059ec10af99",
                                "sense_id": "ad8acf16-1867-3d7c-84bd-bc2757b22273",
                                "text": "Un muscle penniforme déplace proportionnellement une plus lourde charge qu’un muscle fusiforme, mais sur une distance plus courte."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a5a4562d-a475-46ff-aae3-dd6733479268",
                        "source_entry_id": "90fce422-3454-3d14-ad82-b2bea773b980",
                        "target_lang_word": "penniform",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "penniform",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ae3c777-87cb-31b0-8912-7843a3c0e9a5",
                                        "entry_id": "ce781668-6884-32e1-a679-e842dd05910f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Feather-shaped."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a40b7a9f-f80a-400c-9b49-995523ed5e90",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae3c777-87cb-31b0-8912-7843a3c0e9a5",
                                                "text": "Penniform symbols were inscribed on the wall of the cave."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "penniform",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2338897-a336-36ca-a563-898228957c08",
                                        "entry_id": "13efbd72-b985-3859-bee4-bded4e5fa778",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A symbol that is shaped like a feather."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03966bc7-eb26-4da5-9f1d-550233804c98",
                                                "sense_id": "e2338897-a336-36ca-a563-898228957c08",
                                                "text": "Even in the palaeolithic periods symbols abound such as cup markings, tectiforms, penniforms, groups of dots, rectangles, lattice designs, symbolic vulvas, and so on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca68259e-5365-435a-b393-529cacec6d47",
                                                "sense_id": "e2338897-a336-36ca-a563-898228957c08",
                                                "text": "Startlingly, the much earlier Blombos cave engravings clearly fit neatly into several of Von Petzinger's categories: lines, crosshatching, cruciforms, penniforms, and perhaps others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cd8fba5-3f4f-402d-8f28-c8a79b2846f6",
                                                "sense_id": "e2338897-a336-36ca-a563-898228957c08",
                                                "text": "The symbols she found ranged from dots, lines, triangles, squares and zigzags to more complex forms like ladder shapes, hand stencils, something called a tectiform that looks a bit like a post with a roof, and feather shapes called penniforms. In some places, the signs were part of bigger paintings. Elsewhere, they were on their own, like the row of bell shapes found in El Castillo in northern Spain (see picture below), or the panel of 15 penniforms in Santian, also in Spain.[…]The earliest known penniform is from about 28,000 years ago in the Grande Grotte d’Arcy-sur-Cure in northern France, and later appears a little to the west of there before spreading south. Eventually, it reaches northern Spain and even Portugal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
